# Ensure all files are checked into the repo with LF line endings and checked 
# out with LFs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ANSI art is BINARY, not text that happens to use CRLF.
#
# It was `text eol=crlf` -- store LF, hand out CRLF. That round-trips for real text and CORRUPTS
# these: a .ans ends with a 128-byte binary SAUCE record, and any 0x0A inside it is
# indistinguishable from a line ending once git has normalised the file. On checkout git turns
# every LF into CRLF, inserting a CR into the middle of the metadata and shifting every byte
# after it. Measured: 20 of 40 sampled files check out at a DIFFERENT SIZE than they were
# committed at, and 153 of 200 tracked .ans hold a bare LF this rule corrupts.
#
# `-text` means git stores and returns the exact bytes. The art still USES CRLF row endings --
# unchanged, still required -- it just is not git's job to manufacture them.
**/*.ans -text
**/*.icy -text
**/*.xb  -text

# Override GitHub language detection
*.bas linguist-language=qb64
*.bi linguist-language=qb64
*.bm linguist-language=qb64
*.frm linguist-language=qb64
*.otf binary
